// Eppillos, in the pit. Freed at night, with the guard bribed or by stealth.
=== start
[quest pit done] -> gone
[quest pit none] -> stranger
He looks up from the bottom of the pit. Mud to the knees, hands tied in front of him, a split lip going black. "Who are you? Did my father send you?"
-> hub

=== stranger
A young man at the bottom of a pit looks up at you, and then down again. He has stopped shouting a while ago. Whatever he did, it's somebody else's business.
* Leave him. -> END

=== gone
The pit is empty except for the mud.
* Leave. -> END

=== hub
* [!night] "Not in daylight. Tonight." -> wait
* [night, quest pit=guard_paid] "The guard's looking the other way. Here's the rope." -> freed
* [night, !quest pit=guard_paid, !flag pit_alarm, roll sneak -15] "Quiet. I'm getting you out." -> freed | caught
* "Hold on." -> END

=== wait
"Tonight." He nods, and keeps nodding, as if he can't stop. "Tonight. Yes."
* Leave. -> END

=== freed
~ set pit_closed; quest pit done_freed done; honor 3; renown 1; xp 75
He comes up the rope hand over hand, faster than you'd think with his wrists tied, and you cut the cords at the top. For a moment he just breathes the cold air.

"South gate's watched. I'll go over the cliff on the west side. My great-uncle's people are in the hills." He grips your arm. "Tell my father. Tell him I'm sorry, and I'd do it again."

And he's gone into the dark, and the pit is empty.
* Go. -> END ~ leave

=== caught
~ set pit_alarm; standing arverni -10
The rope is halfway down when the guard turns round. He shouts, and somewhere a dog starts barking, and a light comes on in the granary. You're gone before anyone sees your face, but they'll double the watch now. That way is closed.
* Get away. -> END
